  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International has federal contract obligations totaling $3.2B in FY2026 to date across 902 awards, with an average award size of $3.6M. Obligations are down 26.6% year over year. Obligations peaked in FY24 at $4.5B and have declined to $3.2B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.3B, followed by the General Services Administration with $1B. Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services are the largest markets, with $1.2B and $1.1B respectively. Other notable markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $244M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $118M. The current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights where Science Applications International is concentrated by agency and NAICS market during the FY2026 to date period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of Science Applications International in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.3B. The General Services Administration obligates $1B. Other top buyers include the Department of Homeland Security with $205M and the Department of the Treasury with $166M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services account for the most obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market at $1.2B, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $1.1B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences categories account for $244M and $200M respectively, while Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $118M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International has federal contract obligations totaling $3.2B in FY2026 to date. The company recorded 902 awards with an average award size of $3.6M, and obligations are down 26.6% year over year. Historical obligations were $4.5B in FY24, $4.4B in FY23 and FY25, $3.9B in FY22, and $3.3B in FY21."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.3B. The General Services Administration obligates $1B. Other buyers include the Department of Homeland Security ($205M), the Department of the Treasury ($166M), and the Department of State ($127M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services are the top markets, with obligations of $1.2B and $1.1B respectively. Additional offerings showing material obligations include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences ($244M and $200M where separately listed) and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing ($118M)."
    },
